Here is the root cause:
The root cause of the bug was the use of dentry pointers in the eventfs inode without holding a reference count on those pointers. This led to potential dangling references when dentries were removed, as the eventfs implementation attempted to maintain coherence with dentries going away by hooking into the '.d_iput' callback, which was not reliable due to the lack of proper ordering with respect to lookups. This fundamentally broken approach could result in accessing invalid memory, leading to crashes or undefined behavior.

